# Deliberate binary breaks in 1.12.0, relative to 1.11.0. See the release note in README.md.
#
# ShortestPaths.undiscoveredEdges and .undiscoveredVertices duplicated the methods of the same
# names on Graph, with the receiver moved into a parameter, and nothing called them anywhere:
# not src/main, not the specs (ShortestPathsSpec exercises Graph's pair), not the Java facade.
# Deleted on tidy/robin1. See #106, which also asks whether Graph's surviving pair should be
# renamed, since `filteredAdjacencies(_ => true)` filters nothing.
#
# They are in published 1.10.0 AND in published 1.11.0, so removing them is a real break against
# both: the release carrying this is 1.12.0, not 1.11.1. Under PVP, 1.11.x -> 1.12.0 is a major
# bump, so the break is permitted.
#
# THESE FILTERS DO NOT RETIRE. sbt-mima reads every *.backwards.excludes in this directory
# whatever it is named, so this file stays in force until somebody deletes it. Delete it at the
# 1.12.0 post-release, when previousRelease moves to 1.12.0. See #107.
#
# The lines below are MiMa's own suggestions from the failing run, not hand-written.

ProblemFilters.exclude[DirectMissingMethodProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.gryphon.traverse.ShortestPaths.undiscoveredEdges(com.phasmidsoftware.gryphon.core.Traversable,java.lang.Object,scala.util.Random)scala.collection.immutable.Seq")
ProblemFilters.exclude[DirectMissingMethodProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.gryphon.traverse.ShortestPaths.undiscoveredEdges$default$3(com.phasmidsoftware.gryphon.core.Traversable,java.lang.Object)scala.util.Random")
ProblemFilters.exclude[DirectMissingMethodProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.gryphon.traverse.ShortestPaths.undiscoveredVertices(com.phasmidsoftware.gryphon.core.Traversable,java.lang.Object,scala.util.Random)scala.collection.immutable.Seq")
ProblemFilters.exclude[DirectMissingMethodProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.gryphon.traverse.ShortestPaths.undiscoveredVertices$default$3(com.phasmidsoftware.gryphon.core.Traversable,java.lang.Object)scala.util.Random")

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# #106: Graph.undiscoveredEdges renamed to adjacentEdges, and Graph.undiscoveredVertices
# deleted outright.
#
# Neither name described what it returned. `undiscoveredEdges` was
# `filteredAdjacencies(_ => true)`, which filters nothing: it returned every adjacent edge,
# discovered or not. The name came from a design in which the caller tracked visited state;
# the traversal engine took that over and manages it through VisitedSet, and the name stayed
# behind.
#
# `undiscoveredVertices` is deleted rather than renamed because Traversable.adjacentVertices
# already does the job, and does it correctly. The deleted method read `black` off the edge,
# but a two-way triplet stores a second, `flipped` adjacency at the far end whose far vertex
# is `white` -- so reading `black` answers v itself for half the adjacencies of an undirected
# graph. It hid that behind a `collect` admitting only AttributedDirectedEdge, the one kind
# never stored flipped since DirectedGraph passes bothWays = _ => false, and so returned Nil
# on undirected graphs instead of wrong answers. adjacentVertices reads each adjacency's own
# `vertex`, which is the correct end in both cases.
#
# Used by ShortestPathsSpec but by nothing in src/main, so this is a rename and a deletion
# rather than a behaviour change for the library itself. It IS a binary break against
# published 1.10.0 and 1.11.0, which is why it belongs in 1.12.0.
#
# The lines below are MiMa's own suggestions from the failing run, not hand-written.

ProblemFilters.exclude[DirectMissingMethodProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.gryphon.core.AbstractGraph.undiscoveredEdges(java.lang.Object,scala.util.Random)scala.collection.immutable.Seq")
ProblemFilters.exclude[DirectMissingMethodProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.gryphon.core.AbstractGraph.undiscoveredEdges$default$2(java.lang.Object)scala.util.Random")
ProblemFilters.exclude[DirectMissingMethodProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.gryphon.core.AbstractGraph.undiscoveredVertices(java.lang.Object,scala.util.Random)scala.collection.immutable.Seq")
ProblemFilters.exclude[DirectMissingMethodProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.gryphon.core.AbstractGraph.undiscoveredVertices$default$2(java.lang.Object)scala.util.Random")
ProblemFilters.exclude[DirectMissingMethodProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.gryphon.core.Graph.undiscoveredEdges(java.lang.Object,scala.util.Random)scala.collection.immutable.Seq")
ProblemFilters.exclude[DirectMissingMethodProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.gryphon.core.Graph.undiscoveredEdges$default$2$(com.phasmidsoftware.gryphon.core.Graph,java.lang.Object)scala.util.Random")
ProblemFilters.exclude[DirectMissingMethodProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.gryphon.core.Graph.undiscoveredEdges$default$2(java.lang.Object)scala.util.Random")
ProblemFilters.exclude[DirectMissingMethodProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.gryphon.core.Graph.undiscoveredVertices(java.lang.Object,scala.util.Random)scala.collection.immutable.Seq")
ProblemFilters.exclude[DirectMissingMethodProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.gryphon.core.Graph.undiscoveredVertices$default$2$(com.phasmidsoftware.gryphon.core.Graph,java.lang.Object)scala.util.Random")
ProblemFilters.exclude[DirectMissingMethodProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.gryphon.core.Graph.undiscoveredVertices$default$2(java.lang.Object)scala.util.Random")
